# ── Schema snapshots must round-trip byte-for-byte ─────────────────────────
#
# This repo has core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, so git rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. pg_dump emits pure LF. Without this rule the committed
# snapshot comes back with all ~7,800 lines changed, a freshly generated dump
# never matches it, and `npm run schema:check` reports drift on a perfectly
# clean database — forever. A check that always cries wolf is a check somebody
# switches off.
#
# Proven, not assumed: committing the dump without this rule changed its hash
# from 602b8add to bd24ad67; with it, the hash survives the round trip intact.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the snapshot directory. A blanket `*.sql` rule would
# renormalise all 143 existing migration files and produce a diff touching
# every one of them.
mobile/supabase/schema/** -text
